# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# QUESTRA AI — FRONTEND ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your actual values.
# On Vercel, set these in Project → Settings → Environment Variables.

# Gemini AI — the API key lives on the BACKEND (GEMINI_API_KEY env var).
# All generation calls are proxied through {VITE_BACKEND_URL}/api/ai/generate.
# Only set this for local development without a backend (direct calls expose
# the key in the browser bundle — never set it in production builds):
# VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
# Google OAuth Client ID (public — safe to expose)
# Get from: https://console.cloud.google.com/
VITE_REACT_APP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=462752093792-7qe3v01bs6a25v8ldsttt9cenvg1mtg1.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Backend URL — use your Render service URL in production
VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://quesgen-ai-2.onrender.com
